question.text:
Consider the shift-reduce parsing process for the input string $\textbf{id * id $\$ $ }$ . The grammar used for this parse is the expression grammar:
$$
\begin{aligned}
& E \rightarrow E+T \mid T \\
& T \rightarrow T * F \mid F \\
& F \rightarrow(E) \mid \text { id }
\end{aligned}
$$
Let $x$ be the total number of shift operations performed during the parse, and $y$ be the total number of reduce operations performed (excluding the final "accept" action).
Calculate the value of $\frac{x}{y}$ up to $2$ decimal places.
